        "original_id": "19554fc4-5c6f-5eec-8fca-576475a298d0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tom Kristensen, Petter Solberg, David Coulthard, Pascal Wehrlein, Hamble James Leacock\n- Events: 2014 Race of Champions, Nations' Cup, individual contest, 24 Hours of Le Mans\n- Places: Bushy Park, Barbados\n- Topics: motorsport records, birthplace\n\nFacts:\n- Hamble James Leacock was born in Barbados, where his father was a slaveholder.\n- Tom Kristensen won six consecutive 24 Hours of Le Mans races from 2000 to 2005.\n- Tom Kristensen holds the record for the most 24 Hours of Le Mans wins with nine.\n- Bushy Park in Barbados hosted the 2014 Race of Champions later in 2014.\n- The Nordic team of Tom Kristensen and Petter Solberg won the Nations' Cup at the 2014 Race of Champions.\n- David Coulthard won the individual contest at the 2014 Race of Champions by beating Pascal Wehrlein 2–0 in the final.",
